# Product essentials

## Shared

::: checklist [type="progress" id="shared"]
[x] Marketing version defined {id="shared.marketing-version"}
[x] Build id and channel surfaces defined {id="shared.build-id"}
[x] Changelog and README entry points {id="shared.docs"}
[x] CI and tag artifact workflows {id="shared.ci"}
[x] Debug dump redacts document content {id="shared.redaction"}
:::

## GUI and CLI

::: checklist [type="progress" id="shells"]
[x] About, Help, debug dump, and update status {id="shells.support"}
[x] DUI/Dew software/headless composition path {id="shells.headless"}
[x] Windows native host entry point {id="shells.windows-host"}
[x] CLI version, help, and smoke path {id="shells.cli"}
[ ] Signed Windows installer and uninstall entry {id="shells.signed-installer"}
[ ] Verified package-manager update channel {id="shells.updates"}
[ ] macOS and Linux native window hosts {id="shells.other-hosts"}
:::

## Deferred honestly

The v0.1 packaging script creates a portable Windows zip and checksums. It is
not an installer, is not signed, and does not implement automatic updates.
